This is how sounds are structured in HE games:

Quick easy descriptions:

- TLKB: Indicates a TALK bank. At the start of the file. Only contains the size of the chunk + child chunks.
- TALK: Voice samples. Will usually contain SBNG, SDAT and HSHD. Only contains a size of the chunk + child chunks.
- SBNG: Voice sync.
- SDAT: Contains sound data and the size of the chunk.
- HSHD: Contains info about the sound, such as sample rate and bits per sample.

- SONG: Indicates a SONG bank. At the start of the file. Only contains the size of the chunk + child chunks.
- SGHD: This is at the start of the file and says how many songs there are. This is used to calculate where the data point starts (size * SGEN size).
- SGEN: This is an "entry" at the start of the file. It gives a song id, position and size of the DIGI chunk that it references.
- DIGI: This chunk indicates a song. Will usually contain HSHD and SDAT.